3. Design Decision & Alternative Complexity Analysis
Design Choice: Combined Boolean conditions (and/or) inside a flat if–elif–else chain are
preferable to nested if statements. A flat structure reads like a tariff schedule without horizontal
indentation drift ("arrow anti-pattern"), making boundary modifications or slab insertions
straightforward without untangling nested else clauses.
Alternative Approaches: Using Python 3.10+ match–case with guard clauses (case u if 101 <= u
<= 200 and has_ration:) or a lookup list of (upper_limit, condition_fn, decision) tuples
yields O(k) worst-case time across k slabs. While if–elif–else and match–case require O(1)
auxiliary space, the tuple lookup table consumes O(k) memory to store the slab definitions.
