2. Parameter Usage, LEGB Scope & Alternatives
Parameters: Use positional parameters for mandatory inputs (
standard fallbacks (
order=None , 
item ), default parameters for
tax_rate=0.05 ), and keyword arguments at call sites for
optional flags or overrides (
discount=5.0 ).
Scope Rules (Local, Nonlocal, Global): Variables assigned inside a function default to local scope.
Modifying a module-level variable requires 
global , while modifying an enclosing function's
variable inside a nested function requires 
nonlocal . Mutating globals is avoided in software
design because it introduces hidden state coupling, making testing and concurrency unsafe.
Alternative Designs: Passing an explicit caller list (
cart = []; add_item("Tea", cart) ) or
using a closure factory (
make_order() returning an inner 
add(item) function) both achieve
O(1) amortized time per item and O(m) space for m items, though closures incur slight extra
memory overhead per customer for the function/cell wrapper.
